model {
  extend basalt.poolRuntime {
    metadata {
      constraint "Generation sends own submission tracking. Accepted HTTP responses and attempted WebSocket generation writes make later local failures terminal unknown; only positively validated provider refusals permit failover. Credential, refresh and token-count calls remain auxiliary. Preserve native error envelopes, correlation identity, pre-write recovery and retained Home funding behavior. Gemini zero-output responses retain the upstream credential cooldown exemption, but submission ownership suppresses upstream credential rotation after acceptance because the generation outcome is unknown."
    }
  }
}
